    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 3723: Maximize Sum of Squares of Digits (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given two positive integers num and sum. A positive integer n is good if it has
                exactly num digits and the sum of its digits is exactly sum. The score of a good integer n is
                the sum of the squares of its digits. Return, as a string, the good integer n that achieves
                the maximum score. If there are multiple possible integers, return the maximum one. If no
                such integer exists, return an empty string.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: num = 2, sum = 3<br>
                Output: "30"<br>
                Explanation: There are 3 good integers: 12, 21, and 30. Their scores are 1^2 + 2^2 = 5,
                2^2 + 1^2 = 5, and 3^2 + 0^2 = 9. The maximum score is 9, which is achieved by 30.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    string maxSumOfSquares(int digits, int target) {
        if (target &gt; 9 * digits) return "";

        string result;

        while (digits-- &gt; 0) {
            int value = min(9, target);
            result += char('0' + value);
            target -= value;
        }

        return target == 0 ? result : "";
    }
};</code></pre>
